    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classCase" kindref="compound">Case</ref> entity for the <computeroutput>clinics_prescriptions</computeroutput> table (a visit&apos;s prescriptions). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A thin value type that binds the generic Case/Entity CRUD machinery to one table. The table&apos;s primary key is the visit id (a foreign key to <computeroutput>clinics_visits</computeroutput> with ON DELETE CASCADE), so there is at most one prescriptions record per visit. SQL generation is inherited; this class fixes the table name and the visit table used to resolve the owning clinic during create-authorisation. The static getPermissionsQueryFor* helpers are taken as function pointers by <ref refid="classapi_1_1v2_1_1PermissionManager_1a7ca637c16b64d7ebc2e29acc0f366cf0" kindref="member">PermissionManager::canCreate</ref>/canRead/canUpdate/ canDelete for api::v2::Case_t T. Registered as <ref refid="classClinicController" kindref="compound">ClinicController&lt;Prescriptions&gt;</ref> under the <computeroutput>prescriptions</computeroutput> serviceType. Ownership: the data wrapper is copied into <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref> and is const thereafter; no mutable state and no locking of its own. Copy and move are deleted by <ref refid="classCase" kindref="compound">Case</ref>. <simplesect kind="note"><para>No default constructor: <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref> needs a data wrapper to build statements from. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classCase" kindref="compound">Case</ref>, <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref>, <ref refid="gatekeeper_8cpp_1ae17e951f1dc80a8e4920571ebe9f3c21" kindref="member">PermissionManager</ref>, <ref refid="classClinicController" kindref="compound">ClinicController</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
